          "forensics_seed0.disturbance.pitch_before_push_rad",
          "forensics_seed0.support.com_margin_before_push_m",
          "forensics_seed0.support.xcom_margin_before_push_m",
          "controller.stand.stand_hip",
          "controller.stand.stand_knee",
          "creature.body.thigh_length"
        ],
        "competing": [
          "The lean could be due to the standing pose (stand_hip = 0, stand_knee = 0) combined with the mass distribution.",
          "Changing stand_hip or stand_knee targets could shift the COM forward, but the foot is still very short.",
          "Increasing thigh_length or shank_length would move the hip higher and might change the lean, but also changes leg length and inertia."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "H3",
        "mechanism": "The balance controller (ankle torque from torso pitch) is too weak or slow to bring the extrapolated COM margin back positive after the push. The peak pitch rate (0.471 rad/s) and peak pitch (0.158 rad within 1 s) show a growing oscillation that the controller cannot damp.",
        "evidence": [
          "forensics_seed0.disturbance.peak_pitch_rate_within_1s_rad_s",
          "forensics_seed0.disturbance.peak_abs_pitch_within_1s_rad",
          "forensics_seed0.disturbance.time_of_peak_pitch_s",
          "forensics_seed0.failure.fall_after_push_end_s",
          "controller.stand.balance_gain",
          "controller.stand.kd"
        ],
        "competing": [
          "Increasing balance_gain could generate larger ankle torque, but demand is already only 2% of the limit, so authority exists.",
          "Increasing kd (damping) might reduce the pitch rate, but the support polygon size is the hard constraint.",
          "The controller cannot create support where none exists; if the extrapolated COM is past the foot edge, no ankle torque can recover it."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "proposals": [
    {
      "id": "P1",
      "hypothesis": "H1",
      "category": "morphology",
      "edits": [
        {
          "param": "foot_length",
          "op": "scale",
          "value": 2.0,
          "target": "both"
        }
      ],
      "retune_controller": false,
      "prediction": {
        "metric": "forensics_seed0.support.support_length_before_push_m",
        "direction": "increase",
        "expected_change": "from ~0.008 m to ~0.016 m (doubled)"
      },
      "tradeoffs": "Larger feet increase support polygon width, directly improving static and dynamic margins. May increase foot mass slightly (leg_density fixed) and change contact geometry. No controller retuning.",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "verification": "Check that min_xcom_margin_after_push_m becomes less negative and xcom_margin_recovered_s becomes non-null in new seeds."
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "hypothesis": "H2",
      "category": "control",
      "edits": [
        {
          "param": "stand.stand_hip",
          "op": "set",
          "value": 0.05,
          "target": "both"
        },
        {
          "param": "stand.stand_knee",
          "op": "set",
          "value": -0.1,
          "target": "both"
        }
      ],
      "retune_controller": false,
      "prediction": {
        "metric": "forensics_seed0.disturbance.pitch_before_push_rad",
        "direction": "increase",
        "expected_change": "from -0.118 rad toward 0 (less backward lean)"
      },
      "tradeoffs": "Shifting the standing pose forward moves the COM forward relative to the foot, improving pre-push margins. However, the foot is still very short (0.05 m), so the absolute improvement in com_margin is limited. May increase knee torque demand in steady stance.",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "verification": "Check com_margin_before_push_m and xcom_margin_before_push_m become less negative or positive in new seeds."
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "hypothesis": "H3",
      "category": "control",
      "edits": [
        {
          "param": "stand.balance_gain",
          "op": "scale",
          "value": 1.25,
          "target": "both"
        },
        {
          "param": "stand.kd",
          "op": "scale",
          "value": 1.25,
          "target": "both"
        }
      ],
      "retune_controller": false,
      "prediction": {
        "metric": "forensics_seed0.disturbance.peak_pitch_rate_within_1s_rad_s",
        "direction": "decrease",
        "expected_change": "from 0.471 rad/s to ~0.35 rad/s (more damping)"
      },
      "tradeoffs": "Higher balance_gain and kd increase ankle torque response and damping, potentially reducing pitch growth rate. But ankle demand is already far from saturation (0.02), so authority exists. The fundamental limit is the support polygon; if xcom_margin stays negative, no amount of ankle torque can recover. This proposal alone is unlikely to prevent falls.",
      "confidence": 0.3,
      "verification": "Check peak_pitch_rate_within_1s_rad_s decreases and xcom_margin_recovered_s becomes non-null in new seeds."
    }
  ]
}

